            "text": "Assume L1: D>0, fix s, and assume L2: 0<s<D. N001 gives H^s(E)=∞. By the supremum definition of H this means F001: for every finite M>0 there exists δ>0 with H^s_δ(E)>M. In addition, contents increase as δ decreases, since a smaller scale allows fewer covers. Thus such a bound remains true at every smaller positive scale.",
